A||||9||Bill H||Question for those with turbos||||1||
Z||000000||Bill H||03-27-2001||11:15 PM||||How hot do your cars run, engine temp that is. Does anyone have cooling issues? And why not, how fast 0-60 if you know. I'll settle for est. time but no fairy tails(0-60 3.1). Thank you all for your time.||||reg||1
Z||000001||c m west||03-27-2001||11:40 PM||||Our 3.4 TDC 86 SE with a Garrett T3 has a temp usually around 210 degrees in bumper to bumper traffic, and 180 - 190 in steady driving<P> best times have been 11.99 at LACR here in CA - but that was 2 years ago - and before the upgraded fuel management system.<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||03-27-2001||11:45 PM||||11s, never seen a SBC do that, hmmm....||||reg||12
Z||000003||gixxer||03-28-2001||12:14 AM||||The turbo itself is watercooled, but no cooling problems. Pretty normal really.<BR>0-60 prob'ly in the low to mid 6's, as I am in 3rd gear already.<BR>1st gear is pretty useless and just exercises the rev limiter.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||03-28-2001||01:48 AM||||No cooling problems with my MillerWoods setup, even in SC heat in bumper-to-bumper traffic. Just crank up the AC and chill!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'd say 0-60 in high 5's with the auto tranny. I'd like to see Dennis' turbo setup in his 3.4<BR>That's something I'd like to do someday, but my 2.8 has 54K and runs very strong. Why pull it if it's perfect?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSEt||03-28-2001||02:01 AM||||Any one have a webpage or something showing how to hook up all the watercooler lines etc...  ???  the one that I found is the T~3 Garrett AR .63  and watercooled. Thank's for any help.      Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>       Tyler,Texas||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroSEt||03-28-2001||09:21 AM||||bump to top... sorry<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>       Tyler,Texas||||reg||1
Z||000007||Predator||03-28-2001||11:54 AM||||I have a Design One Systems Stage II turbo kit, and I can't see any difference in the temp guage even in traffic. The heat is more in the compartment, but the engine has never run hot. I am looking into options to cool the engine compartment. I don't really know the 0 - 60 times, but it is a lot better than it was stock. The only problems I have had with 0 - 60 is trying to keep the car straight, because the tires keep breaking lose. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Will||03-28-2001||08:40 PM||||Disconnect the throttle body heating water tubes (you don't need them when running a turbo, and hardly ever need them without one) and run hoses down to the water connections on the turbo. Jues make sure you attach the hoses to the <I>water</I>connections...<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||gixxer||03-28-2001||11:08 PM||||The routing of the water supply as Will suggested isn't the best approach.<BR>The Design 1 kit routes the water lines so that a natural thermo-siphon(sp?)flow occurs after shutdown. This keeps the oil in the turbo housing cooler so it has less chance of coking.<BR>If you want, I could fax you the relevent pages so you could see what I'm taking about.  ||||reg||1
